WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:18.149
As Jill and Ashley hurried off, Henry looked at his friends.

2
00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:22.594
"We'll have to work fast if we want to solve this mystery," he said.

3
00:00:22.595 --> 00:00:26.972
"The ride will probably start up again after those new tires get here."

4
00:00:26.973 --> 00:00:32.694
"Then let's not waste any time," Cole said. "Who should we question next?"

5
00:00:32.695 --> 00:00:38.610
"How about William?" Maggie pointed to the new boy, who was kneeling by his front tire.

6
00:00:38.611 --> 00:00:42.807
"He's one of our suspects. And he's right over there."

7
00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:46.135
The Lemonade Detectives walked over to William.

8
00:00:46.136 --> 00:00:50.975
"Hi," Henry greeted him. "Did your tire get slashed?"

9
00:00:50.976 --> 00:00:56.579
"Yes!" William scowled. "And it was really expensive."

10
00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.161
Just then Ms. Hernandez called for everyone’s attention.

11
00:01:00.162 --> 00:01:03.947
"I spoke to Belltown Bikes," she announced.

12
00:01:03.948 --> 00:01:07.879
"They'll be here in about 15 minutes with replacement tires.

13
00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:13.323
The ride will continue once everyone's bike is fixed, so please be patient."

14
00:01:13.324 --> 00:01:16.382
"That doesn't give us much time," said Cole.

15
00:01:16.383 --> 00:01:24.553
Henry nodded. He turned to ask William another question, but the boy had disappeared while Ms. Hernandez was talking.

16
00:01:24.554 --> 00:01:27.219
"That's odd," Henry thought.

17
00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:32.957
Maggie had noticed too. "Hey, where did William go?" she asked.

18
00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:38.540
Cole shrugged. "Never mind. We can't waste time looking for him now."

19
00:01:38.541 --> 00:01:44.006
"Right," Henry agreed. "Let's split up so we can interview more people.

20
00:01:44.007 --> 00:01:49.980
Try to find out who left the picnic area, how long they were gone, and who was with them.

21
00:01:49.981 --> 00:01:53.206
We'll meet back here in 15 minutes."

22
00:01:53.207 --> 00:01:58.588
His friends nodded and hurried off, and Henry looked around.

23
00:01:58.589 --> 00:02:04.376
Who should he talk to first? He saw Tiny and his friends nearby.

24
00:02:04.377 --> 00:02:08.973
"Hi, Henry," Tiny greeted him. "How are your tires?"

25
00:02:08.974 --> 00:02:13.232
"They're fine," Henry said. "What about yours?"

26
00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.694
Tiny sighed.

27
00:02:15.695 --> 00:02:21.725
"I got my front and back tires slashed," he said, pointing to his bike.

28
00:02:21.726 --> 00:02:27.699
"Hey, you're a detective, right? Maybe you can figure out who did this!"

29
00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:30.450
"I'm trying," Henry said.

30
00:02:30.451 --> 00:02:34.701
"I want to figure out who left the picnic area while we were all there."

31
00:02:34.702 --> 00:02:38.018
"Not us." Tiny glanced at his friends.

32
00:02:38.019 --> 00:02:42.315
"But some of the girls we were sitting with went to the restroom."

33
00:02:42.316 --> 00:02:45.826
"Did they all walk there together?" Henry asked.

34
00:02:45.827 --> 00:02:47.897
One of Tiny's friends laughed.

35
00:02:47.898 --> 00:02:52.233
"Of course! Girls always go to the bathroom together."

36
00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:58.429
"Yeah," Tiny agreed with a grin. "That way they can talk about us boys!"

37
00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:04.484
Henry smiled. "Did you notice anyone else disappearing for a long time?"

38
00:03:04.485 --> 00:03:06.819
"No." Tiny shrugged.

39
00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:09.870
"Wait, I did," the other friend said.

40
00:03:09.871 --> 00:03:12.900
"It was that weird guy with the dark glasses."

41
00:03:12.901 --> 00:03:16.573
"You're right," said Tiny's friend with the blond hair.

42
00:03:16.574 --> 00:03:21.835
"He's hard to miss! I think that kid from Valley High left for a while too."

43
00:03:21.836 --> 00:03:25.788
He rolled his eyes. "I don't like him at all."

44
00:03:25.789 --> 00:03:30.496
Just then Daisy walked over. "Hi, Henry," she said.

45
00:03:30.497 --> 00:03:35.783
"Are The Lemonade Detectives trying to solve the case of the slashed tires?"

46
00:03:35.784 --> 00:03:38.053
"Yes," Henry said.

47
00:03:38.054 --> 00:03:40.305
"I just thought of something.

48
00:03:40.306 --> 00:03:44.989
What if it wasn't someone from the ride at all?" Tiny said.

49
00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:49.376
"This is a public park. It could have been anyone."

50
00:03:49.377 --> 00:03:52.308
Daisy shook her head.

51
00:03:52.309 --> 00:03:57.597
"Who would follow us all the way out here just to slash our tires?

52
00:03:57.598 --> 00:04:00.765
Besides I bet I know who did it."

53
00:04:00.766 --> 00:04:03.562
"Who?" Henry asked.

54
00:04:03.563 --> 00:04:09.534
"That guy with the sunglasses," Daisy said. "Nobody knows who he is.

55
00:04:09.535 --> 00:04:14.095
Plus, he was only at the picnic area for a few minutes."

56
00:04:14.096 --> 00:04:16.926
Henry saw a flash of red and gold.

57
00:04:16.927 --> 00:04:22.291
When he looked over, he saw the boy from Valley High School hurrying toward the restrooms.

58
00:04:22.292 --> 00:04:26.797
The other student from Valley High School, Tina, was following him.

59
00:04:26.798 --> 00:04:32.772
"What about Tina?" he asked. "Did anyone notice if she left the picnic area?"

60
00:04:32.773 --> 00:04:36.944
Daisy nodded. "I think I saw her leave for a while.

61
00:04:36.945 --> 00:04:40.337
She’s really nice. Is she a suspect?"

62
00:04:40.338 --> 00:04:48.571
"I'm not sure yet," Henry said. "I need to get all the facts first."

63
00:04:48.572 --> 00:04:55.747
He spent the next few minutes questioning several other people.

64
00:04:55.748 --> 00:04:59.501
Then it was time to meet the other Lemonade Detectives.

65
00:04:59.502 --> 00:05:01.021
"What did you find out?"

66
00:05:01.022 --> 00:05:04.127
Henry asked when the three of them were together again.

67
00:05:04.128 --> 00:05:09.852
"Almost everyone saw that guy with the sunglasses leave the picnic area," Maggie said.

68
00:05:09.853 --> 00:05:15.241
"A few people noticed that William left too, but nobody saw him come back."

69
00:05:15.242 --> 00:05:17.718
"Hmm . . . ," said Henry.

70
00:05:17.719 --> 00:05:21.072
"I found out the same thing," said Cole.

71
00:05:21.073 --> 00:05:27.322
"I also found out that Joey and Tina, the two kids from Valley High, left for a while.

72
00:05:27.323 --> 00:05:31.788
What if they planned this prank to make Belltown look bad?"

73
00:05:31.789 --> 00:05:39.047
"Maybe we should talk to them," Henry said.

74
00:05:39.048 --> 00:05:43.678
He and his friends found Joey and Tina standing outside the restrooms.

75
00:05:43.679 --> 00:05:47.813
But they weren't laughing over the prank or plotting more trouble.

76
00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:50.931
Tina looked angry as she glared at Joey.

77
00:05:50.932 --> 00:05:56.645
"I know you slashed those tires, and you'd better confess!" she yelled at him.

78
00:05:56.646 --> 00:06:03.922
"You're making our school look bad!"
